<title>FINLAND: UPM may sell Aamulehti shares.</title>
<headline>UPM may sell Aamulehti shares.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish forest industry group UPM-Kymmene Oy said on Wednesday it had a preliminary agreement to sell 362,324 Aamulehti series I shares to Swedish media group Tidnings AB Marieberg.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale of the shares is contingent on approval of the merger from the annual general meetings of Aamulehti and MTV,&quot; UPM-Kymmene said in a statement, referring to the merger plan revealed on Tuesday between the media group and the domestic broadcaster.</p>
</text>
